1
00:01:41,519 --> 00:01:42,239
Ding Ning

2
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:46,319
What do you think of Chang Yu?

3
00:01:47,519 --> 00:01:48,840
You know Chang Yu?

4
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:51,519
More than just know him.

5
00:01:53,519 --> 00:01:55,840
He was one of the founders of Rujie.

6
00:01:56,319 --> 00:01:59,319
Will you still remember tomorrow

7
00:01:59,439 --> 00:02:01,319
Xu Ruqing, Chang Yu, and I

8
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:02,920
were college classmates.

9
00:02:03,159 --> 00:02:04,560
She's such a great girl.

10
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:06,000
She doesn't want a car or a house.

11
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:06,920
She just wants love.

12
00:02:07,079 --> 00:02:08,000
And he won't even give her that.

13
00:02:08,240 --> 00:02:09,120
He's so stingy.

14
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:10,960
I'm telling you, guys like Zhao Yijie

15
00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:12,479
are destined to be single.

16
00:02:13,639 --> 00:02:15,120
When we were young and reckless,

17
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:17,120
we looked down on the judicial environment back then.

18
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:18,759
We thought it wasn't advanced enough.

19
00:02:18,759 --> 00:02:19,400
And it lacked fairness.

20
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:20,159
I'll work with you.

21
00:02:20,159 --> 00:02:20,919
Work with me.

22
00:02:21,599 --> 00:02:23,520
So when we graduated, the three of us made a pact.

23
00:02:23,879 --> 00:02:25,360
Once we gained enough experience,

24
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:26,960
we'd open our own law firm.

25
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:29,039
A few years later, we did just that.

26
00:02:29,199 --> 00:02:30,680
We named the firm EverVictory.

27
00:02:30,919 --> 00:02:32,400
It was the predecessor to Rujie.

28
00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:36,719
EverVictory. Always victorious.

29
00:02:37,159 --> 00:02:38,800
The first case we took

30
00:02:39,120 --> 00:02:41,439
was helping a farmer in a car crash

31
00:02:41,919 --> 00:02:43,080
get more compensation.

32
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:44,479
He just hit me with his car.

33
00:02:44,479 --> 00:02:45,280
As you know,

34
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:46,639
in legal practice,

35
00:02:47,039 --> 00:02:48,520
"Different compensation for equal lives" is very common.

36
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:51,719
For example, in the exact same car accident,

37
00:02:51,919 --> 00:02:54,120
city residents often receive more

38
00:02:54,199 --> 00:02:56,680
personal injury compensation than rural folks.

39
00:02:57,080 --> 00:02:58,280
But we were indignant.

40
00:02:58,879 --> 00:02:59,919
We wanted to challenge it.

41
00:03:01,039 --> 00:03:03,120
The result of our tireless efforts was

42
00:03:05,599 --> 00:03:08,120
getting him three extra cows.

43
00:03:08,280 --> 00:03:09,039
Thank you.

44
00:03:09,039 --> 00:03:11,240
Thank you, thank you all.

45
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:12,120
Thank you so much.

46
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:13,960
But to our surprise,

47
00:03:14,879 --> 00:03:17,840
the farmers were incredibly satisfied.

48
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:21,039
That made me feel embarrassed.

49
00:03:21,800 --> 00:03:23,879
It was the embarrassment of not being strong enough

50
00:03:24,319 --> 00:03:26,120
and being unable to bring people

51
00:03:26,199 --> 00:03:28,000
true fairness.

52
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:31,759
Even so,

53
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:33,240
we still became

54
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:35,479
heroes to those farmers.

55
00:03:36,919 --> 00:03:38,319
They just wanted to fight for

56
00:03:38,639 --> 00:03:41,039
three more cows or four more sheep.

57
00:03:41,039 --> 00:03:41,840
For this,

58
00:03:42,439 --> 00:03:43,439
some tried to bribe us.

59
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:44,479
No, no. This is too much.

60
00:03:44,479 --> 00:03:45,199
You have to take this back.

61
00:03:45,199 --> 00:03:46,080
Ma'am, you...

62
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:47,319
Some tried to fake evidence.

63
00:03:47,319 --> 00:03:48,879
How could this be fake? It's...

64
00:03:49,319 --> 00:03:50,479
Some even resorted to self-harm.

65
00:03:50,479 --> 00:03:51,599
Hey! Don't actually do it!

66
00:03:51,599 --> 00:03:53,159
Or they would just play the victim,

67
00:03:53,159 --> 00:03:55,039
refusing to pay legal fees.

68
00:03:55,719 --> 00:03:57,240
We gradually turned into

69
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:59,439
convenient consultation tools for their

70
00:03:59,439 --> 00:04:00,520
extortion scam.

71
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:02,439
As for our visible ideals?

72
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:06,000
They were measured by the head.

73
00:04:06,479 --> 00:04:07,199
For example,

74
00:04:07,199 --> 00:04:10,120
if we got a client three extra cows this year,

75
00:04:10,919 --> 00:04:12,080
next year we would work harder

76
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:13,759
to get six.

77
00:04:14,439 --> 00:04:15,680
Our original ideals

78
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:16,959
overnight

79
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:20,319
were disenchanted into something only a Nerd

80
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:23,360
with Nothing better to do cared about.

81
00:04:24,560 --> 00:04:26,480
Besides, we barely had enough to eat.

82
00:04:26,639 --> 00:04:27,839
Running a law firm requires paying for

83
00:04:27,879 --> 00:04:29,720
rent, utilities, and transport.

84
00:04:30,319 --> 00:04:31,360
All of that costs money.

85
00:04:32,199 --> 00:04:33,040
So we decided

86
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:34,639
to stop taking such cases.

87
00:04:35,319 --> 00:04:36,120
For three whole months

88
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:37,560
without a single client, until one day,

89
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,879
a woman showed up.

90
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:43,720
I want to sue an official.

91
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:45,959
She brought us a case.

92
00:04:46,079 --> 00:04:47,279
Nobody expected

93
00:04:47,480 --> 00:04:50,000
it would completely change our fates.

94
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:52,319
He looks like he serves the people,

95
00:04:52,319 --> 00:04:53,639
but he's actually a piece of trash.

96
00:04:53,639 --> 00:04:56,480
What kind of official makes that much money?

97
00:04:56,639 --> 00:04:57,560
The person she wanted to sue

98
00:04:57,560 --> 00:04:59,439
was a deputy county mayor in a poor county.

99
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:01,639
She claimed he was corrupt and took bribes,

100
00:05:01,959 --> 00:05:04,000
and wanted to use her evidence to bring him down.

101
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:06,079
Why did that young widow pay to sue him?

102
00:05:06,199 --> 00:05:07,560
Did they have some bad blood?

103
00:05:10,399 --> 00:05:12,040
You ask a very good question.

104
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:14,920
But back then, even if we were as smart as you,

105
00:05:15,360 --> 00:05:17,319
for the 100,000 yuan to keep our firm alive,

106
00:05:17,319 --> 00:05:18,800
and the vanity of the three of us,

107
00:05:19,240 --> 00:05:21,079
we still would have taken the case.

108
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:28,120
We followed the young widow back to the county.

109
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:30,240
A county leader treated us to dinner that night.

110
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:31,120
Step forward

111
00:05:31,120 --> 00:05:33,800
and expose this disgusting behavior.

112
00:05:34,399 --> 00:05:36,519
He obviously wanted to blow this out of proportion

113
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:38,199
to draw the discipline inspection department's attention.

114
00:05:38,560 --> 00:05:40,480
The next day, we bypassed that county leader

115
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:42,680
to ask villagers about the deputy county mayor's character.

116
00:05:43,079 --> 00:05:44,959
That's when we learned the whole truth.

117
00:05:45,480 --> 00:05:46,759
It turned out this deputy county mayor

118
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:48,600
had spent four whole years

119
00:05:49,240 --> 00:05:51,639
putting together an investment promotion plan.

120
00:05:52,519 --> 00:05:54,439
The plan was set to launch in two months.

121
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:55,680
But if a bribery scandal

122
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:57,199
broke out right at that moment,

123
00:05:57,319 --> 00:05:58,959
the project would have only two outcomes.

124
00:05:59,759 --> 00:06:00,560
First,

125
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:01,639
the project would be aborted completely.

126
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:02,759
Second,

127
00:06:02,759 --> 00:06:04,079
the project would proceed as scheduled,

128
00:06:04,079 --> 00:06:05,800
but all the credit would go to

129
00:06:06,079 --> 00:06:07,079
that county leader

130
00:06:07,079 --> 00:06:08,519
who treated us to dinner that night.

131
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:10,240
So you were treated as a tool.

132
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:11,680
Exactly.

133
00:06:12,399 --> 00:06:14,240
The young widow couldn't find a local lawyer,

134
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:15,079
so she came to us.

135
00:06:15,079 --> 00:06:16,240
What about the evidence of bribery?

136
00:06:17,319 --> 00:06:19,120
As for the 10,000 yuan bribe,

137
00:06:19,759 --> 00:06:21,680
after the deputy county mayor was forced to get drunk,

138
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:23,319
someone shoved it into his hands.

139
00:06:27,959 --> 00:06:28,800
If we don't consider

140
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:30,959
ethics and morals,

141
00:06:30,959 --> 00:06:33,199
you just need to submit the evidence at hand,

142
00:06:33,199 --> 00:06:35,600
and let the procuratorate handle the rest.

143
00:06:38,040 --> 00:06:39,680
So your choice was...

144
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:41,920
We took the young widow's money.

145
00:06:41,920 --> 00:06:42,800
We represent her.

146
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:43,879
Submitting the evidence

147
00:06:43,879 --> 00:06:45,519
is our basic professional ethics.

148
00:06:45,519 --> 00:06:46,560
Professional ethics?

149
00:06:46,839 --> 00:06:49,079
Then you're willingly letting them use you as a tool.

150
00:06:49,519 --> 00:06:51,560
Once this deputy county mayor is dragged down,

151
00:06:51,639 --> 00:06:53,319
the village's investment promotion plan

152
00:06:53,319 --> 00:06:54,240
will be ruined.

153
00:06:54,560 --> 00:06:55,800
What about those villagers?

154
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:57,600
Shouldn't we think about them?

155
00:06:58,399 --> 00:07:00,040
Why don't we just drop this case?

156
00:07:00,040 --> 00:07:01,240
Let someone else worry about it.

157
00:07:01,240 --> 00:07:02,160
Let's not worry about it.

158
00:07:02,160 --> 00:07:03,399
What are you saying?

159
00:07:03,399 --> 00:07:04,680
Hide the evidence?

160
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:07,000
Or run over and help the defendant?

161
00:07:07,399 --> 00:07:07,959
Zhao Yijie.

162
00:07:07,959 --> 00:07:09,000
You're not a savior.

163
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:09,759
You're a lawyer.

164
00:07:09,759 --> 00:07:11,439
You should act according to who you are.

165
00:07:11,439 --> 00:07:12,040
Then let me ask you,

166
00:07:12,040 --> 00:07:13,519
why did you become a lawyer?

167
00:07:13,519 --> 00:07:15,399
Why did we establish this law firm?

168
00:07:16,079 --> 00:07:17,560
From our early startup days until now,

169
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:18,639
are you satisfied?

170
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:20,720
Well, I'm certainly not.

171
00:07:21,160 --> 00:07:21,920
What I imagined at the beginning

172
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:23,439
was nothing like this.

173
00:07:23,720 --> 00:07:25,279
Running around every single day,

174
00:07:25,319 --> 00:07:27,160
eating plain buns and instant noodles,

175
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:28,199
barely getting any sleep...

176
00:07:28,199 --> 00:07:29,199
For what?

177
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:31,040
Just to help people running an accident scam

178
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:32,480
get a few more cows back?

179
00:07:32,480 --> 00:07:33,000
Zhao Yijie.

180
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,240
You aren't the only one with ideals.

181
00:07:34,240 --> 00:07:35,160
We all have ideals.

182
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:36,720
That's why we started a law firm together.

183
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:37,879
But even with ideals,

184
00:07:37,879 --> 00:07:39,079
we need to stay grounded.

185
00:07:39,079 --> 00:07:41,000
We have to fight it out, case by case.

186
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:42,279
You can't just cut corners.

187
00:07:42,439 --> 00:07:44,360
No, no, can you two stop arguing?

188
00:07:44,360 --> 00:07:45,360
I'm not trying to argue with him.

189
00:07:46,439 --> 00:07:47,000
Zhao Yijie.

190
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:48,160
Come on, just talk it out calmly.

191
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:48,879
Ultimately,

192
00:07:48,879 --> 00:07:50,600
you still don't trust the current judicial environment.

193
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:52,000
Even if he is being falsely accused,

194
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:52,519
that will still

195
00:07:52,519 --> 00:07:54,360
be investigated by the Anti-corruption department.

196
00:07:54,360 --> 00:07:55,639
And if that fails, there's the court.

197
00:07:55,639 --> 00:07:56,319
Besides,

198
00:07:56,319 --> 00:07:57,399
what makes you so sure

199
00:07:57,439 --> 00:07:59,319
that other county leaders lack the ability

200
00:07:59,319 --> 00:08:01,040
to secure investment promotion for the county?

201
00:08:02,079 --> 00:08:03,399
Has he lost his memory, bro?

202
00:08:03,399 --> 00:08:04,160
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

203
00:08:04,160 --> 00:08:05,800
We were all at the dinner that day, right?

204
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:06,279
Yes.

205
00:08:06,279 --> 00:08:07,680
You saw how they acted, didn't you?

206
00:08:08,319 --> 00:08:09,879
I saw an opportunity.

207
00:08:09,920 --> 00:08:10,560
An opportunity

208
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:13,240
to do something more long-term and right.

209
00:08:13,240 --> 00:08:13,959
Let me ask you,

210
00:08:14,399 --> 00:08:15,360
what kind of lawyer is

211
00:08:15,360 --> 00:08:17,000
a top-tier, most valuable lawyer?

212
00:08:17,360 --> 00:08:18,560
That requires them to be capable.

213
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:19,279
They need to awaken.

214
00:08:19,279 --> 00:08:20,399
And awaken early.

215
00:08:20,839 --> 00:08:22,360
Why don't we use our power

216
00:08:22,360 --> 00:08:23,800
to become people like that?

217
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:27,839
A lawyer follows rules and maintains order.

218
00:08:27,839 --> 00:08:29,160
Just because you are close to the law,

219
00:08:29,160 --> 00:08:30,680
you can't assume you are the law itself.

220
00:08:30,680 --> 00:08:31,879
You can't transcend the law

221
00:08:31,879 --> 00:08:33,240
to destroy rules and order.

222
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:34,879
Laws are made by people,

223
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:37,240
and anything made by people is bound to have loopholes.

224
00:08:37,399 --> 00:08:39,000
Without disruptors and questioners,

225
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,399
how can our legal system improve

226
00:08:40,399 --> 00:08:41,240
and optimize?

227
00:08:41,240 --> 00:08:43,000
Will our law firm automatically get better?

228
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:43,919
Will it?

229
00:08:43,919 --> 00:08:44,759
I'm hungry.

230
00:08:46,039 --> 00:08:46,919
Are you two hungry?

231
00:08:46,919 --> 00:08:47,720
I'm going to make instant noodles.

232
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:52,759
So you're just a junior lawyer in this small firm.

233
00:08:52,759 --> 00:08:54,840
What right do you have to worry about the state of the world?

234
00:08:54,919 --> 00:08:55,720
Chang Yu.

235
00:08:58,240 --> 00:09:00,320
A lawyer ultimately serves people.

236
00:09:00,399 --> 00:09:01,960
Law is merely our tool.

237
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:03,600
If we utilize it well,

238
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:05,600
we can help and benefit more people.

239
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:07,600
No, law is not a tool.

240
00:09:07,919 --> 00:09:09,440
It is the foundation, the benchmark,

241
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:10,480
the supreme principle.

242
00:09:10,480 --> 00:09:11,639
If you don't even acknowledge principles,

243
00:09:12,039 --> 00:09:13,320
how can you be a legal professional?

244
00:09:14,080 --> 00:09:15,120
Where are you going?

245
00:09:15,120 --> 00:09:15,919
Let him go.

246
00:09:16,639 --> 00:09:18,480
Can't you two just talk this out?

247
00:09:18,480 --> 00:09:19,919
What are you doing?

248
00:09:22,879 --> 00:09:23,679
Ding Ning,

249
00:09:24,919 --> 00:09:26,639
you're actually quite lucky with mentors.

250
00:09:27,399 --> 00:09:29,559
Yu Songfan and I are nothing.

251
00:09:30,639 --> 00:09:33,120
Chang Yu is your best teacher.

252
00:09:35,279 --> 00:09:36,840
He's actually changed quite a bit too.

253
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,240
So what happened in the end?

254
00:09:40,879 --> 00:09:42,639
I took the deputy county mayor's side.

255
00:09:43,200 --> 00:09:44,279
Over the following three years,

256
00:09:44,279 --> 00:09:46,759
that impoverished county successfully secured

257
00:09:46,759 --> 00:09:48,039
several investment promotion projects.

258
00:09:48,039 --> 00:09:49,600
And as he was promoted,

259
00:09:49,720 --> 00:09:52,320
my people and I have been protecting him all along.

260
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:54,799
So,

261
00:09:55,559 --> 00:09:57,840
that deputy county mayor from back then is your...

262
00:09:58,440 --> 00:09:59,080
Yes.

263
00:10:02,120 --> 00:10:03,320
His name is Bi Wenhao.

264
00:10:05,759 --> 00:10:07,600
He's currently the deputy mayor of Jiangliu.

265
00:10:10,840 --> 00:10:11,639
Ding Ning.

266
00:10:12,080 --> 00:10:13,399
In real life,

267
00:10:13,919 --> 00:10:15,360
nothing is purely black and white.

268
00:10:15,559 --> 00:10:17,679
Seemingly unacceptable evils

269
00:10:17,799 --> 00:10:19,639
can actually be used for good.

270
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:20,840
Sophistry.

271
00:10:21,240 --> 00:10:22,320
I protect them,

272
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:24,120
not for profit,

273
00:10:24,639 --> 00:10:25,879
but because I see that,

274
00:10:26,039 --> 00:10:27,799
despite navigating the gray areas,

275
00:10:28,559 --> 00:10:30,080
they have genuinely

276
00:10:30,279 --> 00:10:32,759
and completely changed many bad things.

277
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:36,120
But there are many ways to do good!

278
00:10:36,559 --> 00:10:38,440
Why must you break the law and rules?

279
00:10:38,559 --> 00:10:40,639
No one wants to break the rules.

280
00:10:41,159 --> 00:10:43,080
But when the making and amending of laws

281
00:10:43,679 --> 00:10:45,399
fail to keep up with the times,

282
00:10:45,440 --> 00:10:47,080
if you want things to go smoother

283
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:48,600
and be completed faster,

284
00:10:48,879 --> 00:10:51,879
specific individuals must pay the price.

285
00:10:55,159 --> 00:10:56,200
Have you noticed?

286
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:59,000
In the face of your so-called ideals:

287
00:10:59,399 --> 00:11:00,799
Real people have become

288
00:11:00,799 --> 00:11:01,840
your sacrifices.

289
00:11:02,679 --> 00:11:04,600
You've deviated from your original intention.

290
00:11:10,840 --> 00:11:11,679
I admit it.

291
00:11:12,559 --> 00:11:15,240
So now it's time for you to choose.

292
00:11:18,600 --> 00:11:21,480
Either accept our rules of conduct,

293
00:11:21,879 --> 00:11:24,799
report the Sham Litigation Factory to the procuratorate,

294
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:26,480
and make Ma Tingting and the others take the bait,

295
00:11:26,679 --> 00:11:28,399
or don't follow in my footsteps.

296
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:30,759
Just withdraw from Liang Zidong's case

297
00:11:31,679 --> 00:11:33,799
and become the lawyer you want to be.

298
00:11:36,559 --> 00:11:39,919
We are the ones who truly believe in you,

299
00:11:39,919 --> 00:11:41,000
and value you.

300
00:11:41,559 --> 00:11:43,039
So if you help me this time,

301
00:11:43,039 --> 00:11:44,399
I can guarantee you one thing.

302
00:11:45,639 --> 00:11:46,440
What?

303
00:11:49,399 --> 00:11:50,480
People of every era

304
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:51,799
have their own shelf life.

305
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:53,519
But our group and model

306
00:11:53,519 --> 00:11:55,080
must carry on.

307
00:11:55,919 --> 00:11:57,440
Therefore, each of us

308
00:11:58,000 --> 00:11:59,679
has a successor.

309
00:12:01,639 --> 00:12:02,519
What do you mean?

310
00:12:05,279 --> 00:12:07,159
You're the one I've chosen.

311
00:12:13,159 --> 00:12:14,919
I want to introduce you to Mr. Bi.

312
00:12:15,320 --> 00:12:17,360
You'll no longer be anyone's pawn,

313
00:12:17,600 --> 00:12:19,840
but will become the next generation's Mastermind.

314
00:12:20,799 --> 00:12:22,679
You won't have to follow the rules

315
00:12:22,679 --> 00:12:23,799
in order to break them anymore.

316
00:12:24,559 --> 00:12:25,759
Because when that time comes,

317
00:12:26,879 --> 00:12:28,480
you will be the one making the rules.

318
00:12:29,919 --> 00:12:31,320
I believe your future self

319
00:12:32,600 --> 00:12:35,759
will definitely become darker than me, yet

320
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:39,000
brighter than Yu Songfan.

321
00:12:43,559 --> 00:12:45,080
A perfect person.

322
00:13:07,519 --> 00:13:09,200
The info for the plaintiff and defendant,

323
00:13:09,200 --> 00:13:10,519
you can't get it wrong.

324
00:13:10,519 --> 00:13:11,720
You've been an intern for three months.

325
00:13:11,720 --> 00:13:12,600
You wrote it all backwards!

326
00:13:12,600 --> 00:13:13,559
If I don't dock half a month's pay,

327
00:13:13,559 --> 00:13:14,440
you won't learn your lesson.

328
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:15,200
Hurry up and fix it.

329
00:13:15,279 --> 00:13:16,080
Honestly...

330
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:17,600
Lawyer Chang...

331
00:13:17,879 --> 00:13:18,799
That daughter-in-law of mine,

332
00:13:18,799 --> 00:13:20,480
she's a total bastard!

333
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:20,919
Ma'am.

334
00:13:20,919 --> 00:13:22,879
Stop calling your daughter-in-law a bastard.

335
00:13:22,879 --> 00:13:23,600
Let's get back to the point.

336
00:13:23,600 --> 00:13:26,080
Have them transfer the house ownership quickly, okay?

337
00:13:26,080 --> 00:13:27,000
Transfer the house?

338
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:28,200
You go find her! Find her!

339
00:13:28,200 --> 00:13:28,840
Find her, right?

340
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:29,519
Xiao Luo.

341
00:13:29,519 --> 00:13:30,080
Mentor.

342
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:31,639
Call Uncle Cai right now.

343
00:13:31,639 --> 00:13:32,080
Okay.

344
00:13:32,080 --> 00:13:33,759
Tell him to stop wasting money on a lawsuit.

345
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:35,799
I've looked at their mediation terms.

346
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,000
They're good enough.

347
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:38,120
Go on.

348
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:38,879
Okay, Mentor.

349
00:13:47,039 --> 00:13:49,279
Can't you make it a bit brighter in here?

350
00:13:49,279 --> 00:13:50,639
Trying to save on electricity?

351
00:13:51,120 --> 00:13:52,120
None of your business.

352
00:13:54,279 --> 00:13:55,840
You have to pick a side when it's time.

353
00:13:56,039 --> 00:13:57,279
Trying not to offend either side

354
00:13:57,279 --> 00:13:58,720
just offends both sides.

355
00:13:59,240 --> 00:14:00,039
Have a seat.

356
00:14:00,320 --> 00:14:01,120
I said the same thing

357
00:14:01,200 --> 00:14:03,559
to Zhou Hao when he first went to Rujie.

358
00:14:10,080 --> 00:14:11,360
I recognize that look in your eyes.

359
00:14:12,399 --> 00:14:13,960
You're not here for advice.

360
00:14:14,399 --> 00:14:16,080
Tell me, why are you here?

361
00:14:18,960 --> 00:14:20,480
Just taking a look.

362
00:14:21,279 --> 00:14:22,159
Looking at what?

363
00:14:23,960 --> 00:14:25,759
To see if you still love yelling at people so much.

364
00:14:26,320 --> 00:14:27,320
To see if the neighbors

365
00:14:27,320 --> 00:14:29,480
are here to freeload off your AC and heating again.

366
00:14:36,440 --> 00:14:37,960
I remember when I first graduated,

367
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:39,519
the reason I came here to intern

368
00:14:40,320 --> 00:14:41,600
was because I heard

369
00:14:41,720 --> 00:14:43,879
that for a petty telecom scammer,

370
00:14:44,039 --> 00:14:46,039
you pointed at a judge and cursed them out in court.

371
00:14:46,440 --> 00:14:47,919
That rumor is way too fake.

372
00:14:48,200 --> 00:14:49,440
Why would I curse at them?

373
00:14:49,440 --> 00:14:50,480
And a judge, no less.

374
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:54,679
But they did collude inside and out

375
00:14:54,679 --> 00:14:55,879
and convicted me of perjury,

376
00:14:56,240 --> 00:14:57,399
making me do time for three months.

377
00:14:57,559 --> 00:14:59,320
The Bureau of Justice revoked my license.

378
00:14:59,879 --> 00:15:00,840
That's very gutsy!

379
00:15:00,960 --> 00:15:03,559
Later, the Bar Association appealed for me,

380
00:15:04,120 --> 00:15:05,799
the Political and Legal Affairs Commission mediated,

381
00:15:06,039 --> 00:15:07,480
and the Supervisory department got involved too.

382
00:15:07,480 --> 00:15:08,679
Only then was my name cleared.

383
00:15:08,919 --> 00:15:10,159
Those three months inside

384
00:15:10,399 --> 00:15:11,639
made me figure out a lot of things.

385
00:15:11,799 --> 00:15:12,759
What did you figure out?

386
00:15:12,879 --> 00:15:14,919
You figured out that because you stuck to your ideals

387
00:15:14,919 --> 00:15:16,039
and ended up behind bars,

388
00:15:16,200 --> 00:15:18,360
you don't want young, idealistic lawyers

389
00:15:18,360 --> 00:15:19,679
to repeat your mistakes.

390
00:15:19,720 --> 00:15:21,360
That's why you always knock them down,

391
00:15:21,519 --> 00:15:24,039
forcing them to be realistic, right?

392
00:15:25,559 --> 00:15:28,159
Don't mention flowery words like ideals.

393
00:15:28,159 --> 00:15:28,919
It's not like that.

394
00:15:29,120 --> 00:15:30,039
Everyone has their own fate.

395
00:15:30,840 --> 00:15:32,360
Whether you're successful or not is innate.

396
00:15:32,519 --> 00:15:33,919
I'm perfectly happy living like this.

397
00:15:35,120 --> 00:15:36,360
Not asking for wealth or status,

398
00:15:36,399 --> 00:15:37,519
just peace of mind.

399
00:15:39,120 --> 00:15:40,399
Back during the male nurse case,

400
00:15:40,399 --> 00:15:41,639
why did I do what I did?

401
00:15:42,159 --> 00:15:43,679
It's because in those three months inside,

402
00:15:43,679 --> 00:15:44,720
I figured out

403
00:15:44,720 --> 00:15:45,799
that as lawyers,

404
00:15:45,799 --> 00:15:47,080
we can forge ahead bravely

405
00:15:47,279 --> 00:15:48,519
and abhor evil,

406
00:15:48,519 --> 00:15:49,279
but we cannot

407
00:15:49,279 --> 00:15:50,919
gamble with our clients' interests.

408
00:15:57,759 --> 00:15:59,559
Ding Ning, you are an exception.

409
00:16:00,320 --> 00:16:01,919
We were once mentor and apprentice.

410
00:16:02,759 --> 00:16:04,480
I know you have Nezha's spirit.

411
00:16:05,120 --> 00:16:06,240
I hope whatever you forget,

412
00:16:06,240 --> 00:16:07,480
you never forget one thing:

413
00:16:08,320 --> 00:16:11,600
think clearly about why you became a lawyer.

414
00:16:58,600 --> 00:16:59,279
Go ahead.

415
00:17:01,600 --> 00:17:02,879
The Sham Litigation Factory

416
00:17:03,240 --> 00:17:04,799
is a trap jointly set by

417
00:17:04,799 --> 00:17:06,279
Liang Zidong and Zhao Yijie.

418
00:17:06,559 --> 00:17:08,599
I guess the files inside are half true, half false.

419
00:17:09,359 --> 00:17:10,039
Don't go.

420
00:17:10,480 --> 00:17:11,559
Why can't we go?

421
00:17:12,960 --> 00:17:13,759
I don't know.

422
00:17:14,359 --> 00:17:15,799
I tried getting information out of Zhao Yijie all night,

423
00:17:15,799 --> 00:17:16,599
but he didn't say anything.

424
00:17:17,640 --> 00:17:18,799
But he made A single oversight

425
00:17:18,799 --> 00:17:19,960
and revealed something.

426
00:17:20,559 --> 00:17:21,279
What is it?

427
00:17:22,039 --> 00:17:23,440
In Liang Zidong's case,

428
00:17:23,440 --> 00:17:26,160
on all documents accessible through official channels,

429
00:17:26,519 --> 00:17:27,680
your name is nowhere to be found.

430
00:17:28,160 --> 00:17:30,160
But when Zhao Yijie mentioned the investigation team,

431
00:17:30,160 --> 00:17:30,960
he brought you up.

432
00:17:31,680 --> 00:17:32,480
So...

433
00:17:33,079 --> 00:17:35,279
So Zhao Yijie has a mole on our team.

434
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:39,759
If you want to share information with me,

435
00:17:39,920 --> 00:17:41,359
root out your mole first.

436
00:17:42,839 --> 00:17:43,720
I believe you.

437
00:17:44,759 --> 00:17:47,880
But if the Sham Litigation Factory isn't wiped out,

438
00:17:48,079 --> 00:17:49,640
I won't be able to report back.

439
00:17:49,880 --> 00:17:51,480
And our team investigating Zhao Yijie

440
00:17:51,559 --> 00:17:53,599
and the Fuxia Group's illegal activities

441
00:17:53,640 --> 00:17:54,599
will be disbanded.

442
00:17:54,839 --> 00:17:57,119
Maybe it's because you're always so eager to close the case,

443
00:17:57,400 --> 00:17:58,480
that for the past five years,

444
00:17:58,480 --> 00:17:59,799
you've only been catching a scapegoat

445
00:17:59,799 --> 00:18:00,920
and small fry.

446
00:18:01,559 --> 00:18:02,920
What are you implying?

447
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:08,240
Do you play chess?

448
00:18:10,559 --> 00:18:12,480
The most overlooked piece is the pawn.

449
00:18:12,480 --> 00:18:14,440
To protect the king or other pieces,

450
00:18:14,759 --> 00:18:15,839
it can be sacrificed at any time.

451
00:18:16,319 --> 00:18:17,519
I don't play much.

452
00:18:17,640 --> 00:18:18,720
But I know that

453
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:20,839
Pawns can only move forward, never backward.

454
00:18:21,680 --> 00:18:22,440
Exactly.

455
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:25,759
When a pawn reaches the enemy's back rank,

456
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:27,880
it can transform

457
00:18:28,160 --> 00:18:30,319
into any piece it wants.

458
00:18:30,759 --> 00:18:31,880
Like a queen,

459
00:18:32,519 --> 00:18:33,880
a rook, or a bishop.

460
00:18:36,200 --> 00:18:37,599
So the most overlooked pawn,

461
00:18:37,880 --> 00:18:39,160
as long as it's in the right position,

462
00:18:39,759 --> 00:18:41,799
can be completely unstoppable.

463
00:18:43,839 --> 00:18:45,279
What exactly are you trying to say?

464
00:18:46,319 --> 00:18:47,440
Zhao Yijie promised me that

465
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:49,119
if I came and reported

466
00:18:49,119 --> 00:18:50,359
the Sham Litigation Factory to you,

467
00:18:50,680 --> 00:18:52,480
he would make me his successor

468
00:18:53,119 --> 00:18:54,640
and let me meet his Protective umbrella.

469
00:18:55,920 --> 00:18:56,880
So you're saying

470
00:18:57,839 --> 00:18:58,839
you are that pawn.

471
00:19:00,559 --> 00:19:01,960
Since you have to report back,

472
00:19:02,839 --> 00:19:04,480
let's Feign compliance.

473
00:19:05,079 --> 00:19:07,079
You raid the Sham Litigation Factory as usual,

474
00:19:07,160 --> 00:19:09,079
and push me to Zhao Yijie's back rank.

475
00:19:09,799 --> 00:19:11,519
Once I get concrete evidence,

476
00:19:12,279 --> 00:19:13,279
we'll regroup.

477
00:19:28,519 --> 00:19:29,880
Just mop this floor.

478
00:19:29,880 --> 00:19:30,519
Okay.

479
00:19:32,680 --> 00:19:33,400
Hello?

480
00:19:34,039 --> 00:19:35,960
Go. You need to hurry.

481
00:19:49,839 --> 00:19:51,640
So we follow Zhao Yijie's plan,

482
00:19:52,079 --> 00:19:53,599
let him think he's succeeded,

483
00:19:54,599 --> 00:19:55,640
and lower his guard.

484
00:19:55,839 --> 00:19:58,720
We wait until our operation fails

485
00:19:59,920 --> 00:20:01,400
and we're held accountable,

486
00:20:01,559 --> 00:20:02,720
then we root out the mole.

487
00:20:04,640 --> 00:20:05,279
Exactly.

488
00:20:19,640 --> 00:20:20,359
Lao Kong.

489
00:20:21,200 --> 00:20:21,920
Lao Yu.

490
00:20:22,039 --> 00:20:23,359
So many people are gone.

491
00:20:23,759 --> 00:20:24,720
We're nearing the end, after all.

492
00:20:24,720 --> 00:20:25,720
We don't need that many people.

493
00:20:26,359 --> 00:20:27,160
Let me make you a cup of tea.

494
00:20:27,599 --> 00:20:28,319
Alright, alright.

495
00:20:29,079 --> 00:20:30,119
I only have green tea left.

496
00:20:30,119 --> 00:20:30,920
That's fine.

497
00:20:31,839 --> 00:20:32,559
Lao Kong.

498
00:20:32,799 --> 00:20:34,119
I'm in a hurry. I'll skip the tea.

499
00:20:34,119 --> 00:20:35,200
No, no, no.

500
00:20:35,839 --> 00:20:37,160
Keep me company for a bit.

501
00:20:41,680 --> 00:20:43,000
But what if I can't beat him,

502
00:20:43,960 --> 00:20:45,079
and I get eliminated?

503
00:21:05,839 --> 00:21:06,799
This is at the hospital.

504
00:21:07,400 --> 00:21:10,000
Right, they said it's in the hospital's electrical room.

505
00:21:25,079 --> 00:21:25,880
Crap!

506
00:21:26,839 --> 00:21:27,720
The police are here!

507
00:21:28,039 --> 00:21:28,839
Run!

508
00:21:29,960 --> 00:21:30,720
Why are you running?

509
00:21:30,720 --> 00:21:31,599
Why are you running?

510
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:33,039
Why is everyone panicking?

511
00:21:33,039 --> 00:21:34,000
Don't we have a contingency plan?

512
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:35,640
Get rid of all this stuff.

513
00:21:35,920 --> 00:21:37,000
What are you standing around for?

514
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:37,640
Hurry!

515
00:21:45,519 --> 00:21:46,440
There's no signal.

516
00:21:52,680 --> 00:21:53,920
Their signal is terrible.

517
00:21:55,960 --> 00:21:56,680
Oh no.

518
00:21:58,400 --> 00:21:59,440
Tell them to abort the operation.

519
00:21:59,440 --> 00:22:00,079
Fall back immediately.

520
00:22:00,079 --> 00:22:00,759
What?

521
00:22:01,400 --> 00:22:03,240
It was hard enough getting the arrest warrant approved.

522
00:22:03,240 --> 00:22:05,079
I've deployed every officer in the squad for this.

523
00:22:05,079 --> 00:22:05,839
Captain, I don't have time right now

524
00:22:05,839 --> 00:22:06,559
to explain this.

525
00:22:06,559 --> 00:22:07,960
Please tell them to fall back immediately.

526
00:22:08,160 --> 00:22:08,839
Are you sure?

527
00:22:08,839 --> 00:22:09,480
Positive.

528
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:11,799
Abort the operation.

529
00:22:12,400 --> 00:22:13,200
Abort the operation.

530
00:22:14,119 --> 00:22:14,759
Hello?

531
00:22:16,279 --> 00:22:17,440
We've lost their signal.

532
00:22:17,440 --> 00:22:18,400
We can't reach them.

533
00:22:23,680 --> 00:22:24,440
The computers!

534
00:22:26,680 --> 00:22:27,759
Make it snappy!

535
00:22:48,160 --> 00:22:48,920
Move out!

536
00:22:54,079 --> 00:22:54,680
Xiao Li.

537
00:22:54,839 --> 00:22:56,440
Tell the team leader. Don't report this.

538
00:22:56,480 --> 00:22:57,960
Hurry back. Cancel the operation.

539
00:22:58,279 --> 00:22:58,920
But what if...

540
00:22:58,920 --> 00:22:59,480
Hurry!

541
00:23:27,279 --> 00:23:28,519
Police! Don't move!

542
00:23:28,519 --> 00:23:30,160
Drop what you're holding! Get down!

543
00:23:30,160 --> 00:23:31,039
Get down! Get down!

544
00:23:32,319 --> 00:23:32,920
Get down!

545
00:23:40,400 --> 00:23:42,400
Captain, we found a signal jammer.

546
00:23:43,599 --> 00:23:44,759
All right, report to the City Police immediately.

547
00:23:44,759 --> 00:23:45,519
Turn it off.

548
00:23:45,519 --> 00:23:46,160
Got it.

549
00:24:01,920 --> 00:24:03,480
Chief Ma, on our end...

550
00:24:03,480 --> 00:24:04,279
Cancel the operation.

551
00:24:06,839 --> 00:24:07,640
Why?

552
00:24:08,519 --> 00:24:09,680
Our team leader's family member

553
00:24:10,279 --> 00:24:11,480
is a shareholder of this hospital.

554
00:24:11,640 --> 00:24:13,160
Zhao Yijie just wants the higher-ups

555
00:24:13,160 --> 00:24:14,160
to suspect our team leader,

556
00:24:14,160 --> 00:24:15,960
so they'll completely disband our team.

557
00:24:16,559 --> 00:24:17,480
In other words,

558
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:19,279
we all fell into his trap.

559
00:24:40,079 --> 00:24:40,799
Have some.

560
00:24:45,599 --> 00:24:46,519
What are you so mad about?

561
00:24:48,079 --> 00:24:49,160
I'm here to save you, aren't I?

562
00:24:50,880 --> 00:24:52,119
It's one thing to use me.

563
00:24:52,119 --> 00:24:54,599
Why drag Ding Ning down with you?

564
00:24:54,640 --> 00:24:56,160
This is murder.

565
00:24:56,400 --> 00:24:59,319
You're killing the honest and just Ding Ning,

566
